{# ============================================================================
   THE REPORT FLOW. One route, one POST, one set of step partials — and TWO
   CONTAINERS, chosen by where the filing came from.

   FILING FROM A RECORD IS A DRAWER. When the seam carried a record — another
   module's "file as incident" button, the register's report control with context
   — the flow opens as a slide-over panel with the register legible behind it and
   the source card riding inside it. Context you never lost in the first place.

   FILING FROM NOWHERE IS A PAGE. A deep link, a fresh tab, the dashboard's Report
   button: there is nothing to sit over, so the flow takes the whole page. It
   reloads, it deep-links, it prints, and no click beside it can throw it away.

   WHICH MEANS THE FALLBACK IS FREE. A drawer needs something to be over and a
   record to be about; an address that has neither renders the page instead, so
   this route can never open a drawer over nothing.

   The two containers share every step: the kind, the questions, the things that
   can wait, and the gate are ONE set of partials rendered at two widths.
   ========================================================================== #}
{% extends '@UhifadhiIncident/base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Report an incident — {{ area.name }}{% endblock %}

{# THE FILE PREVIEW's vocabulary, and ONLY where the card actually has
   photographs to open in it. This module does not require the storage bundle —
   a deployment with incidents and no Files hub is a real deployment — so asking
   for that bundle's stylesheet unconditionally would be a 404 on every report
   page in such a host. #}
{% block stylesheets %}
    {{ parent() }}
    {% if sourceFiles is not empty %}
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('bundles/uhifadhistorage/preview.css') }}">
    {% endif %}
{% endblock %}

{% block incident_trail_tail %} <a href="{{ path('incident_dashboard', {uuid: area.uuid}) }}">incidents</a> / report{% endblock %}

{# THE FLOW BRINGS ITS OWN HEADING, in both containers — the page's plate and the
   drawer's panel each carry their own title, so filling the frame's head socket
   would print the heading twice. #}
{% block incident_page %}
    {% set container = prefill.hasProvenance ? '_drawer' : '_page' %}
    {{ include('@UhifadhiIncident/report/' ~ container ~ '.html.twig', {
        controller: '@uhifadhi/incident-module/incident-report',
        area: area,
        categories: categories,
        prefill: prefill,
        chosen: chosen,
        csrfToken: csrfToken,
        errors: errors,
        createUrl: createUrl,
        cancelUrl: cancelUrl,
        behind: behind,
        sourceFiles: sourceFiles,
    }, with_context: false) }}
{% endblock %}
